The '''Shahkirin''' were a [[Sentience|sentient]] [[species]] from the [[Inner Rim Territories]]' [[Shahkir system]]. One Shahkirin was a member of the [[Alliance to Restore the Republic|Rebel Alliance]] in [[2 BBY]], being present at the [[Great Temple|Alliance base]] on the [[moon]] [[Yavin 4]] that [[Standard year|year]]. Another member of the species, [[Yipsit]], grew up on the [[planet]] [[Bestine IV]] and served as a [[Resistance]] [[Resistance technician|mechanic]] at its [[Resistance base (Ajan Kloss)|base]] on the moon [[Ajan Kloss]] by [[35 ABY]].

==Biology and appearance==
The Shahkirin were a [[Sentience|sentient]] [[species]]<ref name="TROS VD" /> [[Homeworld|originating]] from<ref name="Planetnamia" /> the [[Inner Rim Territories]]' [[Shahkir system]].<ref name="Appendix" /> They had two [[Limb|arms]] and two legs,<ref name="TROS">{{Film|IX}}</ref> and a flattened head with a [[tooth]]ed [[mouth]] as well as [[eye]]s on its sides.<ref name="TROS OfficialCollector">[[Star Wars: The Rise of Skywalker – The Official Collector's Edition|''Star Wars: The Rise of Skywalker'' – The Official Collector's Edition]]</ref> The species had a compressible cartilaginous [[skeleton]], and the Shahkirin [[Yipsit]] had [[Color|tan]] skin and gray [[hair]]<ref name="TROS VD" /> and was approximately half the size of an adult [[human]] in height.<ref name="TROS" /> Another Shahkirin was also of comparable size and had similar skin and hair color.<ref name="Messenger">{{Andor|Messenger}}</ref>

==Shahkirin in the galaxy==
[[File:Shahkirin-Messenger.png|thumb|left|300px|A Shahkirin was present at the Rebel Alliance base on Yavin 4.]]
In [[2 BBY]]<ref name="Messenger" /> and [[1 BBY]],<ref name="1 BBY">{{AndorDate|212|an appearance of a Shahkirin at the [[Great Temple|Rebel Alliance base]] on [[Yavin 4]]}}</ref> a [[Goggles|goggle]]-wearing Shahkirin member of the [[Alliance to Restore the Republic|Rebel Alliance]] was present at the [[Great Temple|Alliance base]] on<ref name="Messenger" /> the [[moon]] [[Yavin 4]] of the [[Outer Rim Territories]].<ref name="DB Yavin">{{Databank|yavin-4|Yavin 4}}</ref> Yipsit grew up on the cliff faces of<ref name="TROS VD" /> the Inner Rim<ref name="Appendix Bestine">{{GalaxyMapAppendix}} &mdash; Based on corresponding data for the [[Bestine system]]</ref> [[planet]]<ref name="BH29">[[Bounty Hunters 29|''Bounty Hunters'' 29]]</ref> [[Bestine IV]], which imbued him with an innate confidence related to climbing.<ref name="TROS VD" />

By [[35 ABY]],<ref name="35 ABY">''[[Star Wars: The Rise of Skywalker: The Visual Dictionary]]'' describes the state of [[the galaxy]] up to and during the events of {{Film|IX}}, which ''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]'' dates to [[35 ABY]].</ref> Yipsit, who similarly wore mechanized [[magnigoggles]], served as a [[Resistance technician|mechanic]] at the [[Resistance base (Ajan Kloss)|Resistance base]] on the Outer Rim Territories moon [[Ajan Kloss]]. There, the Shahkirin helped with the refurbishment of<ref name="TROS VD" /> the [[Standard decade|decades]]-old,<ref name="Tantive">{{Databank|tantive-iv|''Tantive IV''}}</ref> 108-[[Foot|feet]]-tall<ref name="ArtMandoS2">[[The Art of Star Wars: The Mandalorian (Season Two)|''The Art of Star Wars: The Mandalorian'' Season Two]]</ref> [[CR90 corvette]]<ref name="Encyclopedia">[[Star Wars Encyclopedia of Starfighters and Other Vehicles (second edition)|''Star Wars Encyclopedia of Starfighters and Other Vehicles'', second edition]]</ref> ''[[Tantive IV]]''. Yipsit would confidently scale the [[corvette]]'s [[armor]]ed [[hull]] and use his small size to crawl into access tunnels that adult humans were unable to enter.<ref name="TROS VD" />

==Behind the scenes==
The Shahkirin species was first mentioned in [[Titan Magazines]]'<ref name="TROS OfficialCollector" /> [[December 19]], [[2019]]<ref name="OfficialCollectorDate">{{TitanComics|url=c/1561-star-wars-the-rise-of-skywalker-official-movie-spe|text=Star Wars: The Rise of Skywalker The Official Collector's Edition Book ''Vol.'' 1}}</ref> [[Star Wars: The Rise of Skywalker – The Official Collector's Edition|''Star Wars: The Rise of Skywalker'' – The Official Collector's Edition]] magazine in a preview of the character Yipsit<ref name="TROS OfficialCollector" /> who would go on to appear in<ref name="TROS" /> the [[sequel trilogy]] film [[Star Wars: Episode IX The Rise of Skywalker|''Star Wars'': Episode IX ''The Rise of Skywalker'']] that was released the [[December 20|next day]].<ref name="YearByYear">''[[Star Wars Year By Year: A Visual History, New Edition]]''</ref> Concept art of Yipsit for the film was done by [[Louis Wiltshire]],<ref name="Art">''[[The Art of Star Wars: The Rise of Skywalker]]''</ref> and the character was portrayed by [[Kiran Shah]].<ref name="KiranShah">{{WebCite|url=https://www.littlekiran.com/wordpress/filmography|text=Filmography &#8211; Little Kiran|work=[https://www.littlekiran.com littlekiran.com]|archivedate=20240823161501}}</ref>

